{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794174494,"nonce":"hde03pfvXjvBheVtWC92CPd5LMM=","title":"An agent rewrites a description without overwriting a concurrent edit","message":"An agent edits a description (or any comment) by a file round trip: `issue get` → the message into a file → the agent edits the file with its own tools → `issue comment edit COMMENT_ID - \u003c file`. The round trip already works but is undocumented, and `comment edit` replaces unconditionally, so an edit made between the agent's get and its edit (a human, a Jira pull) is silently overwritten; only `issue log` keeps it.\n\n## Design\n\nAspects that change: `doc/design/issue.md` (Comments), `doc/design/cli.md` only if its map lists the comment verbs' flags, and `host/quickstart.md`.\n\n1. **`issue get` prints each comment's `message_hash`**: the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the comment's message as stored. It is the version an edit names; computed on output, nothing in the entity or the snapshot changes.\n2. **`issue comment edit COMMENT_ID BODY|- --base HASH`** refuses, writing nothing, when the comment's current `message_hash` is not HASH, saying the comment changed since it was read and to get it again. The check runs inside the write lock on the re-read issue (`IssueCache.Update`), so nothing committed between the check and the write is decided against blind (doc/design/store.md, \"Re-read under the lock\"). Without `--base` the edit replaces unconditionally, as now. HASH is the full hash, not a prefix.\n3. **Starlark is the same API**: `work.issue.comment.edit(id, body, base=None)`, and `work.issue.get` carries `message_hash`.\n4. **The check is against this clone.** An edit made on another clone and not yet pulled is not seen; the two edits merge by the operation order as any concurrent edit does. A content hash, not an operation id: an edit that writes back the same text is no conflict, which is what the writer cares about.\n5. **The quickstart documents the round trip** with `--base`.\n\nNot a patch verb (old/new replacements): with the round trip the agent's own editing tools make targeted edits, and `--base` gives the conflict check, so it would be a second way to do one thing.\n\nOut of scope: the terminal's comment editor passing a base.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["cli","core"],"status":"in-progress","type":"story"}}]}